From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shaynelarocque <shaynelarocque@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:51:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Authoritative netcode

Players under authoritative movement (revival.yml authoritative.mode) get
their gameplay packets buffered per client tick and replayed through the
original handlers at the tick end, in client order, interleaved with the
movement simulation. Physics packets sent to them are wrapped with our own
pings so the server knows the client tick each one was applied before.
The logic lives in gg.hcfrevival.revival.auth; this patch adds the
ServerPlayer.revivalAuth field and one-line calls: pong re-enqueue, the
outbound choke point, flush suspend/resume (per-tick bundles), handler
intercepts, teleport sent/accepted, the connection tick, and the block
change journal in LevelChunk.setBlockState. ServerChunkCache counts
changes to its full-chunk map, so the per-player world view can keep the
chunk of its last block read.

